  "body": "## What\n\nTurning operations (profile rough/finish, bore, groove, part) generate their approach just outside the **part**, ignoring the setup stock. With a bar wider than the part they rapid straight into the bar. Since #103 the post refuses such a program (`RapidInStock`), so the output is safe, but a normal job - rough a 20 mm bar down to a 12 mm part - cannot be programmed.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe turning kernels read the revolved stock envelope: the approach clears the stock's radius (plus the retract clearance), and roughing passes start from the stock, not the part.\n\n## Found by\n\n#103 (the meridian-plane rapid law convicted every lathe fixture whose box stock was larger than its bar).\n",
